--separator='---' stitches multiple -F inputs into one note body
with a divider between them; no fallback is provided here. If it
blows up on an older installation, the fix is to concatenate the
two files before passing them as a single -F.

If the MERGE_MSG append ever stops working (git controls that
file and we are tacking on prose it didn't generate), the
fallback is to include the merge subject line at the top of the
summary file and pass it as -F to git commit directly, or to
commit --no-edit then amend with the enriched message.

"Replay" is an informal umbrella for rebase/cherry-pick — not
standard git terminology. If the inline explanation in Section 1
doesn't make the mapping clear enough, an alternative is to drop
the umbrella and say "rebase or cherry-pick" throughout, or to
model it as cherry-pick since git rebase is mechanically a
sequence of cherry-picks.
